{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_20c34998ce0fbaefa797a2ea97d5b5af26bdc1bd787828918d29490259ecdb51"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Playing saved policies requires extra packages installable via requirements_ma_policy.txt, which pins tensorflow 1.13.1, cloudpickle 0.5.2, baselines 0.1.5, opencv-python, and pytest."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2b4ce1fcaaa9b325110611aeb45939749b51af055d34921db2081379dce1fe64"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Environments are built by starting from a Base environment and adding environment modules (e.g. Boxes, Ramps, RandomWalls) plus wrappers on top."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2ff1c9e4eaa09a45f40438652f7487eb3f3530bc5b0f0ceb2c496c3d7c355c77"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository provides environment generation code accompanying the paper 'Emergent Tool Use From Multi-Agent Autocurricula' and its OpenAI blog post."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44440998770eac8ecfb17e491f7078280ce04c6787646665b97b93b7aa49ab2d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A bin/examine script lets users inspect environments and play saved policies, e.g. passing a jsonnet environment config and an npz policy from the examples folder."},{"claim_ids":["clm_768c102d8d232c9c3804ff7c37e1faddf1832499f0a5c2eb2f5686b2e00625d3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository depends on the separate mujoco-worldgen package, which must be cloned and installed (with its requirements) before installing this repo in editable mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a8a9c847d6a89d12be9b453d73911c6e7b5127902ff84e334dd09a1023878449"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is archived: code is provided as-is with no updates expected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ac82ca8224b13346cfc243ee11ed2dc892d8069ce030a23f59cdb54ae230a169"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Defined environments include Hide and Seek (random rooms, quadrant, food variants), Box locking (Lock and Return, Sequential Lock), Blueprint Construction, and Shelter Construction."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bfd55558b2797e345d4754e919f217eae47040b6d3a52a358dfc8681f15957a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"New objects or dynamics should be added via EnvModule classes (objects/sites, simulator changes) or gym.Wrapper classes (rewards, observations, game mechanics like Lock and Grab) rather than subclassing Base."},{"claim_ids":["clm_db6412a692275e87d37a9a8400d6929cf9aecf2d8f45e48a26f5d0ced59ffd9b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository has been tested only on Mac OS X and Ubuntu 16.04 with Python 3.6."}],"claim_ids":["clm_20c34998ce0fbaefa797a2ea97d5b5af26bdc1bd787828918d29490259ecdb51","clm_2b4ce1fcaaa9b325110611aeb45939749b51af055d34921db2081379dce1fe64","clm_2ff1c9e4eaa09a45f40438652f7487eb3f3530bc5b0f0ceb2c496c3d7c355c77","clm_44440998770eac8ecfb17e491f7078280ce04c6787646665b97b93b7aa49ab2d","clm_768c102d8d232c9c3804ff7c37e1faddf1832499f0a5c2eb2f5686b2e00625d3","clm_a8a9c847d6a89d12be9b453d73911c6e7b5127902ff84e334dd09a1023878449","clm_ac82ca8224b13346cfc243ee11ed2dc892d8069ce030a23f59cdb54ae230a169","clm_bfd55558b2797e345d4754e919f217eae47040b6d3a52a358dfc8681f15957a8","clm_db6412a692275e87d37a9a8400d6929cf9aecf2d8f45e48a26f5d0ced59ffd9b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:13:58Z","created_by_operation":"op_3976619699bc4be8a165dc85aa0dad0b","id":"pg_4f352ec00b7154a4b2f2df2ad3603524","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openai-multi-agent-emergence-environments-readme-md-bafaf1e11e63-df2ad3603524.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c2910ef2b5675a43909e6ba441d0c1f6"],"title":"openai/multi-agent-emergence-environments/README.md @ bafaf1e11e63","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:13:58Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3976619699bc4be8a165dc85aa0dad0b"}
